WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.050
If an illness kept you away from work for months,

2
00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:05.383
how much would be missing each month?

3
00:00:06.483 --> 00:00:10.348
Loan repayments, rent and family costs do not wait.

4
00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:12.678
The sum is simple:

5
00:00:12.922 --> 00:00:16.300
your net income, minus what you would still receive,

6
00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:18.564
minus the cover you already have.

7
00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:21.165
That is the monthly gap.

8
00:00:22.265 --> 00:00:25.445
Check what sickness benefit Social Insurance gives you,

9
00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:29.985
what your employer provides, and how many months your savings would last.

10
00:00:31.085 --> 00:00:31.816
And remember:

11
00:00:31.816 --> 00:00:35.728
personal accident insurance covers accidents only, not illness.

12
00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:40.105
If illness is your worry, ask about disability cover.

13
00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:44.838
Work out your gap with the free tool on avrastro.com.
